         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nNow we understand the reason: multiplying any number by zero always gives zero, that is, **0 × N = 0**. Since all the results are the same, all the dots are on the same horizontal line—at the value zero.\n\nThat is why, when we connect them, our drawing is a **straight, flat line** lying exactly on the horizontal line—the first shape we draw with multiplication!\n\nIn the next classes, we will draw other multiplication tables (by 1, by 2, ...) and discover new shapes: rising lines and even triangles. What do you think the multiplication table of one will draw?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
